---
description: Maya v2 architecture — runtime, skills, SQLite, MCP as an interface
alwaysApply: true
---

Architecture rules:

1. UI must not call external APIs directly. Chat goes through `/api/chat` → Maya Runtime / Sage.
2. MayaRuntime (and Sage) communicate with the permission engine, then tools.
3. Tools are registered through `lib/skills/registry.ts` and `skills/<name>/`.
4. Every tool has an explicit policy in `lib/permissions/policies.ts`.
5. Dangerous tools require confirmation. Shell stays disabled.
6. Brain implementations live behind `lib/core/brain.ts`. Swap Ollama without touching Memory or UI.
7. Structured state (memories, tasks, plans, audit) uses SQLite at `data/maya.db`.
8. Conversations still persist in the vault JSON (`data/maya-memory.json`) until a later migration.
9. Do not introduce PostgreSQL or a vector database unless explicitly requested.
10. MCP (`mcp/server`) is an external interface to Maya, not the internal architecture.
11. Never expose secrets to the model.
12. Never execute arbitrary shell commands.
13. Preserve existing chat, voice, rooms, and smoke behavior during migrations.
14. Prefer wrapping current modules as skills over rewriting the Next.js app as Vite.
15. Offline skills must keep working when Ollama and the network are down.
